		{
			"id": "117627663096068842",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.evilgeniuschronicles.org/@geniodiabolico/117627663041486931",
			"author": {
				"name": "Dave Slusher - Tech/Podcast/Maker Stuff",
				"url": "https://mastodon.evilgeniuschronicles.org/@geniodiabolico",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/117/482/129/010/943/760/original/f148c086eb78ae60.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-16T19:01:38.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Very condensed version of this story.</p><p>Early 2000s we were rolling out a secure e-publishing system. I spec'd it as requiring sustained 2 tx/second, bursts to 10. Implentors freaked out because it did not do 50 transactions a second. Days of phone calls.</p><p>The system rolls out, then I am laid off. In the middle of the TX ID is a counter, so I can tell exactly how many credentials were minted. I requested one every month to see where they were. 200 in the first 18 months.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117627670698558958",
			"parentId": "117627663096068842",
			"url": "https://mastodon.evilgeniuschronicles.org/@geniodiabolico/117627670526262985",
			"author": {
				"name": "Dave Slusher - Tech/Podcast/Maker Stuff",
				"url": "https://mastodon.evilgeniuschronicles.org/@geniodiabolico",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/117/482/129/010/943/760/original/f148c086eb78ae60.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-16T19:03:32.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.evilgeniuschronicles.org/@geniodiabolico\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>geniodiabolico</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Bear in mind, my transactions to read the counter were 10% of those. The thing we argued about for maybe 20 hours over two weeks, the rate they said was necessary in 4 seconds would have served all the transactions that happened in a year and a half.</p><p>Optimism is nice, but sometimes you got to be realistic.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117627680515560241",
			"parentId": "117627670698558958",
			"url": "https://mastodon.evilgeniuschronicles.org/@geniodiabolico/117627680473837247",
			"author": {
				"name": "Dave Slusher - Tech/Podcast/Maker Stuff",
				"url": "https://mastodon.evilgeniuschronicles.org/@geniodiabolico",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/117/482/129/010/943/760/original/f148c086eb78ae60.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-16T19:06:04.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.evilgeniuschronicles.org/@geniodiabolico\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>geniodiabolico</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Also fun, in one of those argument calls when they were saying 2/10 was insufficient, after I was too exhausted for politeness. I asked \"Can anyone on the call explain the significance of those numbers? I can, because I'm the one who created them and I know why. I will concede my argument right now if anyone can explain why those are significant.\" Of course they couldn't. I made my point that they were cargo culting specs that I CREATED AND TELLING ME I WAS WRONG!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		}
